  {
   "n": 33,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0",
   "html": "<p>\n\tThe measured I-V characteristics of a Si diode maintained at room temperature is crudely sketched as shown in figure. Note that the current scale is logarithmic for forward bias and linear for reverse bias. Non idealities exhibited by the characteristics are identified by capital letters. Various possible sources for the deviations from the ideal are listed below the figure. Identify the cause of each non-ideal I-V feature; place the proper source number(s) adjacent to the letters on the sketch and select the correct option(s):</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d3/d34c1a2e901b146d52b1.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t1. Photogeneration<br />\n\t2. Thermal recombination in the depletion region<br />\n\t3. Avalanche/Zener process<br />\n\t4. Low level injection<br />\n\t5. Depletion approximation<br />\n\t6. Thermal generation in the depletion region<br />\n\t7. Band bending<br />\n\t8. Series resistance<br />\n\t9. <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/07/0783bca1066bf2f278a6.png\" /><br />\n\t10. High level injection</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "A3"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "C2"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "B6"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "D10"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A, B, C, D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(a, b, c, d)<br />\n\t&bull; A: Due to the avalanche/zener breakdown, the diode conducts large current in the reverse direction.<br />\n\t&bull; B: The leakage current flows through the diode when reverse biased due to the diffusion of thermally generated charge carriers in the depletion region.<br />\n\t&bull; C: Due to the recombination by thermally generated carriers, the slope of the IV characteristics reduces.<br />\n\t&bull; D: Due to high level injection, the IV characteristics slope reduces and becomes much flatter at higher currents.</p>"
  }
